### EDI Spec Scrapper - API tests (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
### App must run on :9010. Scraping steps are LIVE and slow.

@base = http://localhost:9010/api

### 1. Health
GET {{base}}/scrapper/health

### 2. Config schema
GET {{base}}/scrapper/config-schema

### 3a. EDIFACT revisions
GET {{base}}/edifact/revisions

### 3b. Message types for a revision (replace D96A with any revision from 3a)
GET {{base}}/edifact/message-types/D96A

### 3c. X12 revisions
GET {{base}}/x12/revisions

### 3d. X12 transaction sets (replace 4010 with any revision from 3c)
GET {{base}}/x12/transaction-sets/4010

### 4. SSE scrape - watch progress events stream in the response pane
GET {{base}}/scrape?standard=EDIFACT&revision=D96A&messageType=INVOIC

### 5. Execute scrape via POST (returns spec + JSON Schema + BeanIO XML in one shot)
POST {{base}}/scrapper/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "standard": "EDIFACT",
  "revision": "D96A",
  "messageType": "INVOIC"
}

### 6. Get previously scraped result as JSON Schema
GET {{base}}/result/D96A/INVOIC?format=jsonschema

### 6b. Same result as BeanIO XML mapping
GET {{base}}/result/D96A/INVOIC?format=beanio

### 6c. Same result in canonical form
GET {{base}}/result/D96A/INVOIC

### 7. Publish to Azure DevOps (requires ~/.datasabai config - expect failure locally)
POST {{base}}/publish
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "standard": "EDIFACT",
  "revision": "D96A",
  "messageType": "INVOIC"
}
